est move is to discard B8 as it is a single tile not part of any chow or pung in my hand and is less likely to be useful to others, preserving potential melds like W6-W7-W8 and pairs in T3/T9/B1.]\nReason: [Discarding B8 minimizes the risk of aiding opponents while retaining key tiles for forming chows and pairs. Keeping W6, W7, W8 intact supports a potential chow, and retaining T3/T9/B1 allows for pair formation. B8 has low utility for my current strategy.]\nAnswer: Play B8"}
